      "content": "a number of skins sewn together to make a fur lining (Veale 219) | a number of skins sewn together to make a fur lining (Veale 219) (see also pellis) | clearly some kind of fur, but exact meaning unknown | fur | a fur trimming or lining for a garment; a garment trimmed or lined with fur; the hairy skin or pelt of an animal; esp., when prepared for use in clothing (MED s.v. furre n.), here made of foyne wombs (q.v.) | a number of fox skins sewn together to make a fur lining (Veale 219)"
